From: Velle Sinclair <brncomputerhelp@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 14:05:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] WM: recognise synui in the process scan

`gather_wm` looks for a known compositor in /proc first and falls back to
mapping XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP when it finds none. That fallback is the wrong
answer for any compositor whose session exports a DESKTOP name that is not
the compositor's name: it reports the desktop instead of the window manager.

On SynapseOS the session exports XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=SynapseOS while the
compositor binary is `synui`, so the WM row read "SynapseOS (Wayland)" —
naming the operating system in the field reserved for the window manager.
fastfetch, which detects the process, has always said `synui` there.

One more entry in the same list dwl, sway, river and labwc are already in.
Nothing about this is specific to one distribution: it is the same shape as
every other row, and any compositor added to that array gets the same
correction.
---
 fetch.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fetch.c b/fetch.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/fetch.c
+++ b/fetch.c
@@ -1921,7 +1921,7 @@
   if (!wm[0]) {
     static const char *known_wms[] = {"dwl",   "sway",    "river", "labwc",
                                       "weston", "i3",      "bspwm", "openbox",
-                                      "awesome", "dwm",    NULL};
+                                      "awesome", "dwm",    "synui", NULL};
     DIR *proc = opendir("/proc");
     if (proc) {
       struct dirent *ent;
